WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.635
-Our next guest has his
comedy special,

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:07.073
"Jesus Trejo: Stay At Home Son,"
available now on Showtime.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.675
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:12.011
please welcome the very funny
Jesus Trejo!

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:16.015
[ Cheers and applause ]
-What's up, everybody?

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:18.551
My mom had her
first Zoom doctor meeting.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.919
I thought that was interesting.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.720
And she's not tech savvy,
so I sat here.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.423
Mom's here.
We're looking at the laptop.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.158
Thing's done. I close it.
I look to my mom.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:26.859
I go, "Mom, what did you think?"

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.162
And she looks at me and goes,
"Who was that guy?"

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.867
Adorable.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.100
Everything is so different.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.205
Like, the roles, for me,
switched during this time.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.540
During quarantine,
everything switched.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.375
Like, I'm the parent,
and my parents feel like

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.643
they're the kids.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.278
Like, my mom has never been
that active before.

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:47.413
Like, "Can I go outside?"

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:50.750
"No, you can't go outside.
You'll get sick."

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.018
"Can I go outside for
a little bit?"

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.786
"No, you can't do that."

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.054
"Please? I want to go outside."

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.222
I'm like, "Mom, you can't."

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.990
And then my little heart,
as a parent, just broke.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.427
I'm like, "Alright,
you can go outside,

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:04.997
but stay where
I can see you, please.

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:06.598
Don't go too far.

00:01:06.598 --> 00:01:08.400
If you see somebody,
you run back in the apartment."

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.704
"Okay, I can do that."

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.306
But I used this downtime to do
everything I wanted to do

00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:15.575
and I never got a chance to do.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:18.377
Like, I read some books.
I saw some movies.

00:01:18.377 --> 00:01:21.313
I cleaned my belly button.
That was cool.

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:24.751
Had the cubic zirconia in there.
Yeah.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.385
Yeah, I even cleaned
my refrigerator.

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:27.420
It felt good.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.520
-Whoo!
-Yeah, thank you.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:29.956
And I realized something.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.758
I realized I've been working on
the same bottle of mustard

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.726
since I was a kid.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:38.030
Like, this bottle has been part
of my life a long time, man.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.465
And I don't even know
if it's bad or not

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.835
'cause it's mustard, right?

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.269
That's what it
tastes like, I guess.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.606
I think we got into
mustard too early.

00:01:47.606 --> 00:01:52.144
We didn't let them
fully invent it.

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:53.279
Think about mustard.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.880
Think about mustard
for a little bit.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.982
Yellow mustard,
spicy mustard, Dijon mustard.

00:01:56.982 --> 00:01:59.385
Guys, keep going. You're close.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.091
If you ever tasted mustard
and it was delicious,

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.927
that's honey mustard for sure.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:12.898
And honey is doing all the
lifting in that relationship.

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:13.900
Yeah, man.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.568
Did you guys know that mustard

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:19.304
was initially invented
to clean jewelry?

00:02:19.304 --> 00:02:22.575
That's not true,
but you believe it

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:26.212
'cause you know what
it tastes like.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.080
Mustard is the only condiment
that you can, like,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.949
spill on yourself,
and people love to point it out

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.684
and ruin your day.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:32.852
Like, "Hey, man,
you got mustard on your shirt."

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.754
You're like, "Oh, dang it, man."

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:35.755
"Have a good one."

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:38.191
"Screw you, man."

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.827
But if you ever feel lonely,
you want to make some friends,

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:43.996
put a little mustard
on your shirt, hit the town.

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:45.331
Just wait.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.999
Like, "Hey, man,
you got mustard on your shirt."

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:49.068
You got to act surprised.
"Oh, dang it, man.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.937
What's your name?
My name is Jesus Trejo."

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:53.739
Friendship made.

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:57.844
Here's a question.
Is every deli famous?

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:03.683
I saw them open
a brand-new deli,

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:06.719
and it already said
"World famous."

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.721
What I wanted to say was,
"Hey, deli, relax.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.123
Enjoy the journey, man.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:14.393
You'll get there.
What's the rush?"

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:16.562
Yeah, man. I like food a lot.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:20.199
This is all going to be
food, so -- Alright.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.101
Yeah. I used to be
addicted to cupcakes.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.869
I used to be really, really
addicted to cupcakes.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:24.903
I ate one every day.

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:28.640
Took Sundays off
'cause diabetes.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.942
Now I'm into muffins.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.678
I feel like the older you get,
your palate becomes

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:33.879
a little more refined, you know?

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:37.816
And a muffin is just
a brave cupcake, you know?

00:03:37.816 --> 00:03:39.152
It got to the point
where it realized

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.586
it didn't need
sprinkles or frosting

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:42.855
and it would be delicious.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.256
I love a muffin, man.

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:45.724
Favorite part about the
muffin -- taking the paper off,

00:03:45.724 --> 00:03:48.061
the little corduroys,
you know...

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.231
Just seeing the muffin
all vulnerable right there,

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:55.168
just chillin',
stretch marks on the side.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:59.305
I'm like, "I like that, muffin."

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.240
Muffin looking like
it's been wearing

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:05.110
jeans and a tight belt all day.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:08.180
You got to relax, man.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.215
I had hot dogs recently.

00:04:10.215 --> 00:04:12.952
I don't want to brag, but I had
hot dogs with my folks.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:17.056
And, yeah,
I was excited about it.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.257
And my dad's like,
"Do we have mustard?"

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.358
I'm like, "Hell yeah.

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:21.961
You'll see
the bottle right over here.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.128
And he came back.

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:25.131
He's like,
"Hey, man, this is bad.

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:26.365
Water came out."

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:27.633
I was like, "Dad,
you got to shake it.

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.902
You got to boot it up.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.370
You got to let it know
you're about to use it.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.538
You surprised it.

00:04:36.074 --> 00:04:40.546
Let somebody squeeze you,
see if water doesn't come out.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.749
You weren't ready, right?"

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.583
He's like, "No. It's bad.
It got brown spots."

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.586
I'm like, "It's deli mustard
now -- world famous."

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.320
Thank you, guys. That's my time.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.923
Appreciate you. Thank you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:51.991
-Jesus Trejo!

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:55.261
For more info,
go to jesustrejo.com.

